From: ImmortalWrt Builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: keep iptables/ip6tables core with the iptables option

Linux 6.12.113 moved the legacy sockopt interface and eval loop behind the
new hidden symbols IP_NF_IPTABLES_LEGACY and IP6_NF_IPTABLES_LEGACY, and both
net/ipv4/netfilter/Makefile and net/ipv6/netfilter/Makefile now key the
ip_tables.o / ip6_tables.o objects off those symbols instead of
IP_NF_IPTABLES / IP6_NF_IPTABLES.

The new symbols are only selected by the individual match/target options, so
a configuration that enables the iptables core alone (OpenWrt ships
kmod-nf-ipt and kmod-nf-ipt6 as standalone packages) no longer builds
ip_tables.o and ip6_tables.o. The kmod packages then fail to install with
"ERROR: module ... is missing".

Give both symbols the same default as their parent option so enabling the
iptables core again implies the legacy interface, restoring the 6.12.112
behaviour while keeping the option to turn it off explicitly.

--- a/net/ipv4/netfilter/Kconfig
+++ b/net/ipv4/netfilter/Kconfig
@@ -14,4 +14,5 @@
 config IP_NF_IPTABLES_LEGACY
 	tristate
+	default IP_NF_IPTABLES
 
 config NF_SOCKET_IPV4
--- a/net/ipv6/netfilter/Kconfig
+++ b/net/ipv6/netfilter/Kconfig
@@ -10,4 +10,5 @@
 config IP6_NF_IPTABLES_LEGACY
 	tristate
+	default IP6_NF_IPTABLES
 
 config NF_SOCKET_IPV6
